<section class="why" id="why">
  <div class="section-header">
    <h2>Why Tiny Steps works for ADHD</h2>
    <p>Built by someone who understands the gap between knowing and doing.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="reasons-grid">
    <div class="reason">
      <div class="reason-number">01</div>
      <h3>Task paralysis is real</h3>
      <p>
        When a task feels big, the ADHD brain shuts down. It's not laziness — it's
        a neurological response to overwhelm. Tiny Steps removes the overwhelm by
        making the first action absurdly small.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reason">
      <div class="reason-number">02</div>
      <h3>Starting is the hardest part</h3>
      <p>
        Research shows that once people with ADHD begin a task, they can often
        sustain focus. The problem is initiation. Our AI makes step one so easy
        ("stand up," "grab your phone") that you bypass the initiation barrier.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reason">
      <div class="reason-number">03</div>
      <h3>Transition steps matter</h3>
      <p>
        Most productivity apps skip the "walk to the kitchen" or "open your laptop"
        steps. For ADHD brains, those invisible transitions are where momentum
        dies. Tiny Steps includes every single one.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reason">
      <div class="reason-number">04</div>
      <h3>Dopamine drives everything</h3>
      <p>
        Each completed step gives you a small hit of accomplishment. The progress
        bar fills. The confetti explodes at the end. These aren't gimmicks — they're
        the neurochemical feedback your brain needs to keep going.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reason">
      <div class="reason-number">05</div>
      <h3>No judgment, ever</h3>
      <p>
        Tiny Steps never uses words like "just," "simply," or "easy." Every step is
        written with the understanding that what seems trivial to others can feel
        monumental. Your experience is valid.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reason">
      <div class="reason-number">06</div>
      <h3>History builds confidence</h3>
      <p>
        Every task you complete is saved. On hard days, scroll through your history
        and see proof that you can do things — you've done them before, one tiny step
        at a time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .why {
    max-width: 1120px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 6rem 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--stone-200);
  }

  .section-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .section-header h2 {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--stone-900);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .section-header p {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--stone-500);
    max-width: 480px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .reasons-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 2.5rem 3rem;
  }

  .reason {
    padding: 0;
  }

  .reason-number {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--amber-500);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .reason h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--stone-800);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .reason p {
    font-size: 0.925rem;
    color: var(--stone-500);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .reasons-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
